  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on counting how many outcomes in each lottery exceed the unweighted average of all outcomes (1225 Euros). Both lotteries have one such outcome above this threshold (2500 and 2400 respectively), so the reason would not prefer one over the other. The individual, however, bases their choice on the higher potential gain (2500 vs 2400) and the small difference in winning probabilities. Although the mention of '100€ mehr gewinnen könnte' (could win 100€ more) aligns with attention to higher outcomes, the reasoning is not based on comparing outcomes to an average, nor on counting how many outcomes exceed such a threshold. Instead, it reflects a common 'maximax' or 'aspiration level' heuristic, focusing on the best possible outcome and its probability. The individual does not reference any average outcome or perform a comparison involving all outcomes' mean. Therefore, the core mechanism of the decision reason (using the average of all outcomes and counting how many exceed it) is absent in the verbal report. The similarity in considering higher payoffs is superficial and does not imply use of the specific rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
